# built by CI and release from frontend source; committed copies go stale
# NOTE: frontend/dist is deliberately NOT ignored. install.sh falls back to the
# committed dist when npm is unavailable (--no-frontend, or a failed toolchain
# install), so the built assets must stay tracked. Ignoring the directory while
# the files remain tracked is worse than not ignoring it: vite's emptyOutDir
# deletes the tracked assets and writes new hashed ones that the ignore rule
# then hides, so a routine `git add -A` commits an index.html pointing at
# assets that are absent from the repo.
